  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decent employment for youth in Cambodia - phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The joint United Nations Decent Employment for Youth in Cambodia (DEY) programme phase 3 (DEY III)  brings together the combined expertise, skills and resources of four participating UN organizations (PUNOs) to achieve the overall objective:  By 2028, more youth in Cambodia are in decent and productive employment. The Participating UN Organizations (PUNOs) are the International Labour Organization (ILO, Convening and Administrative Agency and host of DEY Coordination), the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO), the United Nations Children#s Fund (UNICEF) and the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO). This third phase of the programme (DEY III) will be implemented during the four-year period 01 March 2024 # 28 February 2028. The second phase of this project is SAP 190397 - Decent Employment for Youth in Cambodia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Joint Programme DEY</narrative>
  </participating-org>
